      "username": "phantaskippy",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-02-04T01:22:09.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Jackhandle + Squall:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>You would deal damage to all non-hero targets (Squall), so you choose the first target to be hit, and turn that damage into all target damage.</p><p>Then you pick the second target for Squall to hit, and turn that into all non-hero target damage.</p><p>Then you pick the third target for Squall to hit. . .</p><p>and so on until Squall runs out of targets to aim at.</p><p>I actually mark which ones I've aimed at in these cases.</p><p>The first time I ran across it was with Writhe's attacka &nbsp;target, that target attacks all non-hero targets. (Writhe Attacks Fixer, who goes crazy)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Similarly Jack Handle you would pick a target for Squall, then Crowbar would hit a second, repeat the same way.</p>",
      "post_number": 14,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:05:29.252Z",
